        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people, whey is the better single protein powder: it is absorbed fast, carries more leucine, mixes thin and costs about $1.49 per 25 g in the big ON tub. Casein earns its place for one job, slow overnight protein, plus puddings and baking, at almost the same price per gram in ON's 4 lb tub.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do not overthink the choice. Hit your daily protein target first, pick whey for daytime and post-workout, and add casein before bed only if it helps you get there. If dairy bothers your stomach, switch to a whey isolate, and if you are a tested athlete, buy a powder with a named sport certification.
          </p>
